\n```\n$ accept/4.2-play-loop.py RUNS/m1-20260901 --transcript transcripts/m1-20260901\nPASS  transcript-chain     1 segment(s)\nPASS  advance-invariants   113 advances within policy      -\u003e 2 FAIL / 7 PASS / 2 WARN\n\n$ accept/4.2-play-loop.py RUNS/m1-20260901 --transcript 'transcripts/m1-20260901*'\nPASS  transcript-chain     5 segment(s): m1-20260901 -\u003e -s00 -\u003e -s01 -\u003e -s02 -\u003e -s03\nFAIL  advance-invariants   two consecutive 0-tick advances (wedge rule violated)\n                                                            -\u003e 3 FAIL / 6 PASS / 40 WARN\n```\n\n**That contrast is the finding.** Reading only the head — 21.7% of the run — flips a hard failure to PASS and hides 38 warnings. The wedge-rule violation is this run's own play defect, but it was invisible to the audit the cap forced.\n\n**Acceptance 4 — cap re-justified and documented.** `rwa/README.md` §\"The 999-step cap, and segments\". The justification is better than the issue asked for: 999 is the *width of the zero-padded counter every consumer sorts on* — `1000-ping` sorts before `999-ping`, so widening silently reorders every transcript on disk. The old code said \"1000 steps\" in its message and refused at 999.\n\n**Acceptance 5 — `rwa/selftest.sh`:** `255 passed, 0 failed` (from the repo root), and `accept/4.2-play-loop.py --selftest` -\u003e `SELFTEST PASS`.\n\n\n- **No bench, at all.** Every result above is `fakebench.py` and synthetic roots. A live rotation mid-run has not happened, and this issue's defect arose in a live run. The orchestrator accepts this: the whole failure is client-side and the file half never touches Verse.\n- The five real `transcripts/m1-20260901*` directories were **read only**; their `meta.json` links are still absent on disk and would be derived on the next real call against that run root.\n\n\n- **`1de2fbe` filed (p2):** `rwa/selftest.sh` reports **190 passed, 28 failed** when run as `./selftest.sh` from `rwa/`, which is what its own README says to do. Reproduced by the orchestrator. §13 resolves `templates/*.ir.json` against cwd while every other path resolves from `$0`. Pre-existing on `main`, not introduced here.\n- **Worktree staleness, and it is systemic.** This worker's worktree was cut at `c429dda` — **97 commits behind `main`**, not the ~20 it estimated. It caught this and rebased, which is the only reason the merge was a clean fast-forward; unrebased, it would have reverted `accept/4.2-play-loop.py` by 426 lines and silently dropped the newer `advance-discipline` and `advance-wakes` checks. Every worker dispatched with worktree isolation this round is exposed to the same thing, and the orchestrator now verifies `git merge-base --is-ancestor main \u003cbranch\u003e` before every merge.","files":null}]}